  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "Last summer \\(30 \\%\\) of the birds living on Town Lake were geese, \\(25 \\%\\) were swans, \\(10 \\%\\) were herons, and \\(35 \\%\\) were ducks. What percent of the birds that were not swans were geese?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(20\\)",
    "B": "\\(30\\)",
    "C": "\\(40\\)",
    "D": "\\(50\\)",
    "E": "\\(60\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The requested percentage uses the birds that are not swans as its whole. These birds account for\n\\[\n100\\%-25\\%=75\\%\n\\]\nof all the birds. All the geese belong to this group.\n\nBecause the given percentages refer to the same original total, that total cancels when we divide. The percentage of non-swans that are geese is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{75}\\cdot100\\%=40\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(40\\%\\), choice C.",
